pi-phone ports parts of sim-use (https://github.com/lycorp-jp/sim-use, at commit
c02295edfd2f442249b869096dda3dc7bfcd308d), changed for pi-phone (each file says so in
its header):

- src/server/phone-outline.ts: from Sources/AndroidBackend/Normalizer/
  AndroidOutlineRenderer.swift, AndroidClassifier.swift, AndroidListDetector.swift
  and Sources/SimUseCore/ElementType.swift, in TypeScript, cut down and numbered as
  pi-phone's browser numbers a page's controls.
- android/app/src/main/java/io/piphone/PiAccessibility.java and PhoneControl.java:
  from bridge/app/src/main/java/com/linecorp/simuse/devicebridge/
  (SimuseAccessibilityService.kt, handler/TreeHandler.kt, GestureHandler.kt,
  InputHandler.kt, CaptureHandler.kt, KeyboardStateHandler.kt), in Java, reached
  through pi-phone's own server instead of an HTTP server on the device.
- android/app/src/main/res/xml/phone_control_service.xml: from
  bridge/app/src/main/res/xml/accessibility_service_config.xml.

sim-use's NOTICE also credits AXe and Facebook idb, for its iOS parts: pi-phone
uses none of them.
